
    - there is no obvious cause for its presence
        - it appears to be a thing of purpose, which makes its origin all the more intriguing
        - here I look into it, surveying the potential causes for its presence
    ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
        - [specifically] my aim here is to define a set ⁠X⁠ of potential causal explanantia ⁠x_1,x_2,x_3,\dots⁠
          for the explanandum ⁠y⁠, given as follows

            ⁠\boldsymbol{y}⁠ : The fitness of the cosmos (for use) as a safehold for securing our long-term survival.

    - [now] already cosmology has looked into a phenomenon of similar scope (and pertinence|bearing),
      namely the fine tuning of the cosmos for life, and sought the potential causes for *its* presence
        : ad `scope \(and pertinence\|bearing\)` : namely cosmic (and existential)
        - thus we have predefined [for us] a set ⁠X'⁠ of potential causal explanantia
          for an explanandum that is comparable to ⁠y⁠, namely that of:

            ⁠\boldsymbol{y'}⁠ : The fine tuning of the physical laws, constants and conditions of the cosmos for life.

        !! clumsy rhetoric herein
            | any explanans of the safehold would explain also, one expects, the greater cosmos
                ∵ apparently the safehold is entangled with the cosmos
                    / not a mere appendage
                - other phenomena|explananda that appear so entangled (or physically bound up) include ⁠y'⁠
                    : cf. `already cosmology has looked into a phenomenon of similar scope`
                / maybe a more adept introduction, this
            | making more prominent what is interesting
                | perhaps the greatest strength it has, which might account for its endurance,
                  it owes (by attachment) to its explanantia
                    : re `^*\| (.+)$`s see `^*- ${same}`p
                | ⁠y'⁠ is controversial [as an explanandum] in a way that ⁠y⁠ cannot be
                | in explaining ⁠y⁠, *both* of the [most popular] fine-tuning explanantia figure,
                  and|while *each* has [what appears to be] an indispensible role [to play]
                    - each is necessary [here] but alone does not suffice,
                      where|while both together do [suffice]
        - explanandum ⁠y'⁠ is controversial
            - it faces strong opposition on many fronts
            - perhaps the greatest strength it has, which might account for its endurance,
              it owes (by attachment) to its explanantia
            - these have turned out to be useful for purposes other than explaining ⁠y'⁠
                - e.g., for the two most popular explanantia:
                    - the manifold uses of the idea of a cosmic designer or design
                    - the claim from the multiverse (+ string theory + ‘stranger’ things) chapter
                      of my cosmology handbook that the idea of the multiverse is ‘here to stay’
            - yet another purpose they serve in the present aetiology
        ∴ one may begin by using the predefined set ⁠X'⁠ to define the initial members of ⁠X⁠, as follows

            for( each potential causal explanans ⁠x_i⁠ of set ⁠X'⁠ ) where ⁠i=1,2,3,\dots⁠
                ⁃ divorce ⁠x_i⁠ from explanandum ⁠y'⁠
                    : note : that is all for ⁠y'⁠, fine tuning will not be a premise
                      of the present aetiology
                ⁃ reapply ⁠x_i⁠ instead, mutatis mutandis, to explanandum ⁠y⁠
                ⁃ add the resulting ⁠x_i⁠ to set ⁠X⁠

        - what follows is [based on] the result
    ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
